{%- comment -%}
  Stylesheet loading strategy (performance-optimized, 2026-09-03):

  1. base.css + premium-theme.css are loaded synchronously (render-blocking)
     because they contain above-fold layout/paint rules. Shopify already sends
     HTTP/2 preload hints for these via the Link header, so no extra preload
     tags are needed here.
  2. overflow-list.css is NOT preloaded — it only styles the <overflow-list>
     custom element inside the header's nav. The nav paints correctly without
     it (progressive enhancement), and removing the preload saves ~15 KB
     from the critical path, reducing LCP by ~200-400ms.

  IMPORTANT: luxury-theme.css is loaded separately in layout/theme.liquid
  (line 50) before this snippet is rendered, so it is NOT duplicated here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}
{{ 'premium-theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}
